# `C114` — `subject:locator`. A locator in SUBJECT position is read as a UI locator by the
# matcher-compatibility rule; the identical locator text in ACTION position never reaches that rule
# at all (`D906`). Check-only: every claim here is made by `tflw check`, so it opens no browser.
#
# Three legs, and the middle one is why this is not a diagnostic plant wearing a subject's clothes.
# `C59` rosters `TF042` by reference and grades it on its own probe — `expect status is visible`,
# a *value* subject. Nothing there says a locator is a subject at all. What this file states is
# that the same six-spelling construct is admitted in subject position, judged there, and unjudged
# one word to the left.
test "a locator in subject position is judged, and in action position is not"
  open "/"
  # (1) subject position, incompatible matcher — refused, and the refusal names the KIND.
  expect button "Save" was made
  # (2) subject position, compatible matcher — clean. Without this leg the file would be green if
  #     the checker refused every locator subject, which is the opposite of what the row claims.
  expect button "Save" has count 2
  # (3) action position, the same locator text — the kind rule is never consulted, so no diagnostic.
  click button "Save"
